[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5357106375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122640#issuecomment-5357106375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122640","id":5357106375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP070xw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-20T14:15:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T14:15:04Z","body":"Any thoughts on changing how the `EditorFileSystem` scan works instead (which I guess applies to #122557 as well)?\r\n\r\nWe seem to already be going through the effort of populating the cache/index/whatever in `EditorFileSystem::scan_for_uid`, only to throw it all away once the scan starts. So it's not like these particular UIDs (`default_bus_layout.tres` and main scene) haven't had a chance to be added yet.\r\n\r\nWould it maybe work to have `EditorFileSystem` write any new UID to some temporary cache/index/whatever and then just swap them out at the end of the scan instead? Worst case you could maybe do a lookup in both, if this double-buffering is done in `ResourceUID` instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","re